{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana","id":1122593,"title":"Question About Spirit Arcana","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-29T21:01:10-07:00","id":1122593,"title":"Question About Spirit Arcana","content":"So, I'm new to Mage and I was wondering if there are twilight spirits of disease (i.e. would someone with cancer have like a cancer spirit wandering around?). If so, could a spirit mage hypothetically cure disease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12723-react0rman","name":"react0rman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T21:16:05-07:00","id":1122600,"title":"","content":"There are definitely spirits of disease, and the Spirit Arcanum does hypothetically enable you to use it to cure diseases, but this is a map-is-not-territory thing; if someone has cancer and is ridden by a spirit of cancer, that spirit is not the cause or keystone of that cancer unless it created it through its Influences, which is the domain of especially powerful spirits.<br /> <br /> In practice, a spirit of disease is most able to &quot;cure&quot; its purview in the purely technical sense and/or will require a replacement victim in many cases; dialing down the extremity of a Resonant phenomenon means giving up power and Essence. Getting a hold of a different kind of spirit to either eat it or drive it off is a more involved but less directly fraught approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T21:36:03-07:00","id":1122608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>react0rman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana#post1122593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm new to Mage and I was wondering if there are twilight spirits of disease (i.e. would someone with cancer have like a cancer spirit wandering around?). If so, could a spirit mage hypothetically cure disease?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits only feed on the energy, unless that type of spiritual energy congeals, IE it's in a hospice that gets an abnormal amount of cancer patients. The spirit is just going to be small normally, it can't do much and won't be prone to helping. You'd be better off finding a spirit of health or just using life if you have both life is the simpler and quicker approach then negotiating with spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T21:48:19-07:00","id":1122609,"title":"","content":"Do you mean &quot;will getting rid of the disease spirit help the patient?&quot; I think so. Curing illness by banishing spirits is one of the fundamental parts of animism as a magical practice, so you'd hope that Mage supports it. I would say it's like lifting a weight off the sufferer's back: it won't immediately cure the disease, unlike Life, but it will make recovery much easier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T22:04:52-07:00","id":1122611,"title":"","content":"If the disease is the result of the spirits influence. ie a spirit of measles uses its influences to create measles then getting rid of the spirit wont cure the measles. Could you command the spirit to use its influence to get rid of the measles? Probably but it'd be against its nature and harder than usual. (Though i notice that the influence effects have no &quot;Destroy/remove field so perhaps its not possible for the measles spirit to remove/destroy the measles as its completely against it).<br /> <br /> Other spirits should be able to cure the measles but what ones is up for grabs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-29T22:23:36-07:00","id":1122614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana?p=1122611#post1122611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the disease is the result of the spirits influence. ie a spirit of measles uses its influences to create measles then getting rid of the spirit wont cure the measles.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, no, that's the one specific circumstance where I'd say you <i>can </i>outright end the condition by ending its cause \u2014 you're prying off an extension of the spirit's power, which is part of why Influences bolster a spirit's Clash rolls, particularly in combination with the heightened pressure spirits have to manifest when they're in the material world.<br /> <br /> A spirit riding a person is almost certainly using a Strengthen Influence to allow it to do so, which the case of disease-spirits means sick people get sicker for the duration of the effect but are otherwise no worse off than they'd normally be in those circumstances. A spirit that has outright Created a disease to act as a handhold for its earthly presence cannot sustain that condition without a Manifestation keep its very short clock from ticking down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T09:34:11-07:00","id":1122724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caladriu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana?p=1122609#post1122609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you mean &quot;will getting rid of the disease spirit help the patient?&quot; I think so. Curing illness by banishing spirits is one of the fundamental parts of animism as a magical practice, so you'd hope that Mage supports it. I would say it's like lifting a weight off the sufferer's back: it won't immediately cure the disease, unlike Life, but it will make recovery much easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much how it works. With the exception of some truly powerful beasties, spirits only have the power to empower or alter pre-existing things. So most cancer-spirits can't give you cancer, but they can and will advance an existing cancer or make it resistant to treatment. Removing the spirit won't cure the disease, but it will make the disease much easier to treat.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana?p=1122614#post1122614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, no, that's the one specific circumstance where I'd say you <i>can </i>outright end the condition by ending its cause \u2014 you're prying off an extension of the spirit's power, which is part of why Influences bolster a spirit's Clash rolls, particularly in combination with the heightened pressure spirits have to manifest when they're in the material world.<br /> <br /> A spirit riding a person is almost certainly using a Strengthen Influence to allow it to do so, which the case of disease-spirits means sick people get sicker for the duration of the effect but are otherwise no worse off than they'd normally be in those circumstances. A spirit that has outright Created a disease to act as a handhold for its earthly presence cannot sustain that condition without a Manifestation keep its very short clock from ticking down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most Influence effects have a very limited duration and will therefore go away shortly after the spirit is removed from the premises, but the 5-dot effect has a special clause that allows the entity to permanently create one instance of a thing that falls under its Influence. Such entities also have the ability to permanently Strengthen the disease. So in that rare case, destroying or driving off the spirit off will not cure the disease it created.<br /> <br /> Though in all fairness, if your patient has made an enemy of a Rank 5 disease spirit, they've got bigger problems than whether or not they'll be instantly cured when the spirit goes away.<br /> <br /> <br /> e: Ultimatately the answer to your question is yes: Spirit mages can cure disease. In fact, they can theoretically do almost anything that normally falls under the purview of the other arcana (except Prime). The catch is that they first have to find an appropriate spirit, which can be challenging - spirits of healing, for example, are a lot harder to come by than spirits of trees or buildings. Then you have to either make a deal or press the spirit into servitude, earning you at least one enemy but probably more - spirits are darwinian and hierarchical and don't necessarily have a lot of love for one another, but no ruler likes it when someone else stomps into their fief and starts ordering their servants around.<br /> <br /> And when you do manage to establish relationships with useful spirits, you have to establish a whole lot of them. Even the spirits with the broadest domains will have much narrower Influence than an equivalent mage. You can find spirits of candleflame, forest fire or maybe even Fire itself if you're brave enough, but you'll never find a spirit of Forces - not one beholden to your puny mortal magic, at any rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13628,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","user":"Terrorforge","date":". 07-30-2017, 12:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T13:31:26-07:00","id":1124453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana?p=1122611#post1122611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Though i notice that the influence effects have no &quot;Destroy/remove field so perhaps its not possible for the measles spirit to remove/destroy the measles as its completely against it).</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose Influence 3 with it's ability to make dramatic changes to an Influence would do something similar?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9849-aristarkos","name":"Aristarkos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9849_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T14:42:52-07:00","id":1124483,"title":"","content":"Influence 3 could render the measles harmless, but it wouldn't remove it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T14:54:25-07:00","id":1124487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1122593-question-about-spirit-arcana?p=1124483#post1124483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Influence 3 could render the measles harmless, but it wouldn't remove it.</div> </div> </div> </div>You'd be able to massively reduce its resistance to medication/the immune system, I should think. Possibly even force the virus to exit the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13628-terrorforge","name":"Terrorforge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13628_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"185"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-03T15:21:14-07:00","id":1124496,"title":"","content":"Through the capability of Manipulate you could probably do something like remove it from one person providing you put it into another. Spirits aren't really big on removing their Resonance, but Manipulation allows them to make things chaotic or peaceful in unrealistic manner, causing an illness to become so vicious it gets to killing the victim faster, or so subtle that you wouldn't even notice it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 08-03-2017, 06:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}